[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A  handed finger drumming and rolls.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  • Sampled in a 1 kHz hardware timer ISR (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk212d881555c0f6cc;file:///Users/brett/tmp/drum-synth-with-skills/workspace/drum_synth/main.cpp#L254-L298\u0007TimerCallback\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007) with lock-free queueing to eliminate missed presses\r\n  during OLED updates.\r\n\n  \u001b[1m#### 2. Top Knobs (Master Filter & Saturation Chain)\u001b[m\r\n\n  Wipers are sampled from ADC1, inverted for clockwise increase, and smoothed with an IIR filter:\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mKnob 1 (Chord Vol / \u001b[94;22mD18\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mLow-Pass Cutoff\u001b[m (sweeps 35 Hz to 18 kHz exponentially).\r\n  • \u001b[1mKnob 2 (Chord Filter / \u001b[94;22mD17\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mFilter Resonance\u001b[m (sweeps Q from 5% to 96%).\r\n  • \u001b[1mKnob 3 (Notes Vol / \u001b[94;22mD19\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mHigh-Pass Cutoff\u001b[m (sweeps 20 Hz to 5.5 kHz for DJ-style bass roll-offs).\r\n  • \u001b[1mKnob 4 (Notes Filter / \u001b[94;22mD20\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mMaster Overdrive\u001b[m (warm analog saturation to aggressive punch).\r\n\n  \u001b[1m#### 3. Joysticks & Rotary Encoder\u001b"]
