[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[27A• \u001b[1mKnob 1 (Chord Vol / \u001b[94;22mD18\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mLow-Pass Cutoff\u001b[m (sweeps 35 Hz to 18 kHz exponentially).\n\u001b[76D\u001b[1m2 (Chord Filter / \u001b[94;22mD17\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mFilter Resonance\u001b[m (sweeps Q from 5% to 96%).\u001b[K\n\u001b[67D\u001b[1m3 (Notes Vol / \u001b[94;22mD19\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mHigh-Pass Cutoff\u001b[m (sweeps 20 Hz to 5.5 kHz for DJ-style bass roll-offs).\n\u001b[92D\u001b[1m4 (Notes Filter / \u001b[94;22mD20\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mMaster Overdrive\u001b[m (warm analog saturation to aggressive punch).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[1m#### 3. Joysticks & Rotary Encoder\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mLeft Joystick\u001b[m: X = Pitch Bend (±1.2 octaves), Y = Decay envelope scaling.\n\u001b[73D\u001b[1mRight Joystick\u001b[m: X = Dynamic Cutoff sweep, Y = Dynamic Resonance boost.\u001b[K\n\u001b[69D\u001b[1motary Dial\u001b[m: Master Volume (0% to 100%).\u001b[K\n\u001b[40D\u001b[1mEncoder Push Click\u001b[m: Speaker Amplifier Mute/Unmute toggle (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk1f08adb8549e250c;file:///Users/brett/tmp/drum-synth-with-skills/workspace/drum_synth/gamma_pins.h#L164\u0007PC3\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007), reflected live on the OLED header (\u001b[94m[SPK]\u001b[m vs\r\n"]
