[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A  • \u001b[1mKnob 4 (Notes Filter / \u001b[m\u001b[94mD20\u001b[m\u001b[1m)\u001b[m: \u001b[1mMaster Overdrive\u001b[m (warm analog saturation to aggressive punch).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  \u001b[1m#### 3. Joysticks & Rotary Encoder\u001b[m\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mLeft Joystick\u001b[m: X = Pitch Bend (±1.2 octaves), Y = Decay envelope scaling.\r\n  • \u001b[1mRight Joystick\u001b[m: X = Dynamic Cutoff sweep, Y = Dynamic Resonance boost.\r\n  • \u001b[1mRotary Dial\u001b[m: Master Volume (0% to 100%).\r\n  • \u001b[1mEncoder Push Click\u001b[m: Speaker Amplifier Mute/Unmute toggle (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkce8dfd6b409e320f;file:///Users/brett/tmp/drum-synth-with-skills/workspace/drum_synth/gamma_pins.h#L164\u0007PC3\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007), reflected live on the OLED header (\u001b[94m[SPK]\u001b[m vs\r\n  \u001b[94m[MUT]\u001b[m).\r\n\n  \u001b[1m#### 4. OLED Display (128x64 SSD1306 via I2C1)\u001b[m\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mHeader\u001b[m: \u001b[94m\"GAMMA DRUM\"\u001b[m, speaker state \u001b[94m[SPK]\u001b[m/\u001b[94m[MUT]\u001b[m, and volume \u001b[94mVxx%\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mMiddle Section\u001b[m: 4 real-time horizontal gauge bars and values for \u001b[94mLP\u001b[m, \u001b[94mQ\u001b[m, \u001b[94mHP\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mDRV\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mBo"]
[0.000, "o", "ttom Strip\u001b[m: 7 visual drum pads (\u001b[94m[BD] [SD] [CH] [OH] [LT] [HT] [CP]\u001b[m) that highlight and invert when struck.\r\n\n  \u001b[1m#### 5. USB CDC Connectivity\u001b[m\r\n\n  • Uses \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk81228653c513756d;file:///Users/brett/tmp/drum-synth-with-skills/workspace/drum_synth/gamma_usb.h#L71\u0007gamma_usb::UsbComm\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 on the external USB port (\u001b[94mFS_EXTERNAL\u001b[m).\r\n  • Includes timeout-guarded logging that will never hang the audio loop or freeze the synth if a terminal\r\n  disconnects.\r\n  • Commands \u001b[94m'1'\u001b[m–\u001b[94m'7'\u001b[m fire drum voices remotely; \u001b[94m's'\u001b[m toggles the speaker; \u001b[94m'b'\u001b[m reboots into the Daisy Bootloader.\r\n  ──────\r\n  \u001b[1m### Build & Memory Verification\u001b[m\r\n\n  • Target Archi\r\n⣾  \u001b[90mLoadi\u001b[94mng...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /fork to branch the conversation from an earlier point.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
