[0.000, "o", "fication\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  • Target Architecture: \u001b[94mBOOT_SRAM\u001b[m (entry point \u001b[94m0x24000795\u001b[m in AXI SRAM for the Daisy Bootloader).\n\u001b[93DBinary size: \u001b[1m122 KB\u001b[m (well within the 480 KB SRAM partition).\u001b[K\n\u001b[60DSRAM utilization: \u001b[1m25.48%\u001b[m (125,256 B / 480 KB).\u001b[K\n\u001b[46DDTCMRAM utilization: \u001b[1m23.61%\u001b[m (30,944 B / 128 KB).\r\n\u001b[K\n  When you are ready to connect the Gamma synth via USB, you can flash the binary using either:\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[4C\u001b[38;5;246;3m# Automated bootloader detection & flash:\u001b[m\n\u001b[41D\u001b[38;5;252mpython3 .a\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n⣷ \n\n\n\u001b[?2026l"]
