[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A  \u001b[1m#### \u001b[m\u001b[1m4. OLED Display (128x64 SSD1306 via\u001b[m\u001b[1m I2C1)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  • \u001b[1mHeader\u001b[m: \u001b[94m\"GAMMA DRUM\"\u001b[m, speaker state \u001b[94m[SPK]\u001b[m/\u001b[94m[MUT]\u001b[m, and volume \u001b[94mVxx%\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mMiddle Section\u001b[m: 4 real-time horizontal gauge bars and values for \u001b[94mLP\u001b[m, \u001b[94mQ\u001b[m, \u001b[94mHP\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mDRV\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mBottom Strip\u001b[m: 7 visual drum pads (\u001b[94m[BD] [SD] [CH] [OH] [LT] [HT] [CP]\u001b[m) that highlight and invert when struck.\r\n\n  \u001b[1m#### 5. USB CDC Connectivity\u001b[m\r\n\n  • Uses \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk65db620a50261054;file:///Users/brett/tmp/drum-synth-with-skills/workspace/drum_synth/gamma_usb.h#L71\u0007gamma_usb::UsbComm\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 on the external USB port (\u001b[94mFS_EXTERNAL\u001b[m).\r\n  • Includes timeout-guarded logging that will never hang the audio loop or freeze the synth if a terminal\r\n  disconnects.\r\n  • Commands \u001b[94m'1'\u001b[m–\u001b[94m'7'\u001b[m fire drum voices remotely; \u001b[94m's'\u001b[m toggles the speaker; \u001b[94m'b'\u001b[m reboots into the Daisy Bootloader.\r\n  ──────\r\n  \u001b[1m"]
[0.000, "o", "### Build & Memory Verification\u001b[m\r\n\n  • Target Architecture: \u001b[94mBOOT_SRAM\u001b[m (entry point \u001b[94m0x24000795\u001b[m in AXI SRAM for the Daisy Bootloader).\r\n  • Binary size: \u001b[1m122 KB\u001b[m (well within the 480 KB SRAM partition).\r\n  • SRAM utilization: \u001b[1m25.48%\u001b[m (125,256 B / 480 KB).\r\n  • DTCMRAM utilization: \u001b[1m23.61%\u001b[m (30,944 B / 128 KB).\r\n\n  When you are ready to connect the Gamma synth via USB, you can flash the binary using either:\n\n\u001b[91D\u001b[38;5;246;3m# Automated bootloader detection & flash:\u001b[m\n\u001b[41D\u001b[38;5;252mpython3 .agents/skills/gamma-firmware-flash/scripts/flash_firmware.py drum_synth/build/gamma_drum_synth.bin\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[4C\u001b[38;5;246;3m# Or manu\u001b[m\r\n⣯  \u001b[90mGenerating...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /fork to branch the conversation from an earlier point.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
